  "proof_route": [
    "exists_isCompact_seq_volume_sdiff_eq_zero: cut S by the compact exhaustion compactCovering V m, where the Haar volume is finite, apply MeasurableSet.exists_isCompact_isClosed_sdiff_lt with error (k+1)^-1 to each piece, and reindex the double family by Nat.unpair; infinite volume needs no extra hypothesis",
    "L4: set A n = Set.accumulate C n, compact as a finite union; measure_iUnion_eq_iSup_accumulate (continuity from below, valid for possibly nonmeasurable increasing families) turns the slice measure of the union into the supremum of the slice measures of the A n, each measurable by L3; the remainder S minus the union is Lebesgue-null and u is Lipschitz on it, so L2 makes its slice null at almost every level, and subadditivity plus monotonicity squeeze the slice measure of S between",
    "L5: lintegral_eq_iSup_eapprox_lintegral writes the slice integral as a supremum of simple-function integrals; SimpleFunc.lintegral expands each into a FINITE sum over the range, with Measure.restrict_apply turning the terms into slice measures of the measurable sets S intersect s preimage of c; Finset.aemeasurable_sum and AEMeasurable.iSup preserve AEMeasurable",
    "no parametric-integral theorem is used anywhere, so Measurable.lintegral_prod_right's SFinite requirement on the inner measure never arises",
    "T1: L5 at S = univ, simplified by Set.univ_inter"
  ],
